  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on assessing and comparing the skewness of the two lotteries, favoring the one more heavily weighted toward favorable outcomes (i.e., higher probability on zero). The relevant information includes the distribution of probabilities across outcomes, particularly whether a greater mass is on less negative outcomes. However, the individual instead focuses exclusively on expected value (expected loss), summarizing each lottery by its average outcome. There is no mention or indication of considering how probabilities are distributed beyond their contribution to expectation. The justification is based on a different rule: minimize expected loss, not maximize left-skewness. The reasoning process described does not align with the skewness-based rule. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

